{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Behold, I cut a covenant.</b> That I will go with you. And from what you said, 'and by what shall it be known indeed that I and your people are distinguished?' — the answer to this: 'before all your people I will do wonders.' Another interpretation: 'Behold, I cut a covenant with you' — this is as stated at the end of the matter, 'for upon the basis of these words I have cut a covenant with you and with Israel,' who needed a new covenant because they violated the first covenant. And these are the conditions written from the beginning of 'שמר לך' ('keep for yourself'). And just as he mentioned in the portion of Mishpatim 'את חג המצות תשמור' ('the festival of unleavened bread you shall keep'), so he mentioned it here, because it is a remembrance that on it you went out of Egypt. He also mentioned here the firstborn (פטר רחם), because it too is a remembrance of the exodus from Egypt." "<b>For he is awesome.</b> This is the shining of the face (קרן פנים), about which it says: 'and they were afraid to approach him.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:01:50.583448386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}